There were [1mtwo bugs[22m in the C-to-Rust translation, both in how the BLAKE hash functions were called:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m called with bit counts instead of byte counts (hash.rs + main.rs)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C BLAKE implementation has a quirky API: [38;5;10mblake512_update()[0m and [38;5;10mblake256_update()[0m take [38;5;10mdatalen[0m in [1mbits[22m, but the higher-level C code ([38;5;10mhash_blake.c[0m and [38;5;10mPQCgenKAT_sign.c[0m) passes [1mbyte counts[22m directly to these functions. This is the actual behavior that produces the correct KAT vectors.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translator noticed the bit-based API and "helpfully" multiplied all lengths by 8 when calling [38;5;10mupdate()[0m, thinking this was the correct conversion. But this changed the semantics — the C code hashes only a fraction of the data (e.g., 3 bytes of a 24-byte key when passing [38;5;10mSPX_N=24[0m as bits), and the KAT vectors were generated with this behavior.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix in [38;5;10mhash.rs[0m[22m: Removed [38;5;10m* 8[0m from all 6 [38;5;10mupdate()[0m calls in [38;5;10mgen_message_random()[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message()[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix in [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m[22m: Removed [38;5;10m* 8[0m from all [38;5;10mupdate()[0m calls in the transcript functions ([38;5;10mkat_tr_init[0m, [38;5;10mtr_absorb_label[0m, [38;5;10mtr_absorb_u64[0m, [38;5;10mtr_absorb_bytes[0m). Changed [38;5;10m64[0m → [38;5;10m8[0m where bit counts were used instead of byte counts.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: Wrong buffer offset in [38;5;10mprf_addr[0m (hash.rs)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C code:[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10mblake256(outbuf, buf, SPX_N + SPX_ADDR_BYTES);
[0m[0m[0m
Hashes from [38;5;10mbuf[0][0m — i.e., [38;5;10mpub_seed || addr[0m (56 bytes).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10mblake256(&mut outbuf, &buf[SPX_N..], (SPX_ADDR_BYTES + SPX_N) as u64);
[0m[0m[0m
Hashed from [38;5;10mbuf[SPX_N][0m — i.e., [38;5;10maddr || sk_seed[0m (56 bytes). Same length, completely different data.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix[22m: Changed [38;5;10m&buf[SPX_N..][0m to [38;5;10m&buf[0m to hash from the buffer start, matching the C behavior.[0m[0m
